course: dictionary
lesson: 7760
title: Pure: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pure means not mixed with anything else. A scientist calls a substance pure when it is made of only one thing, like pure water or pure gold. «Salt is spread on icy roads because salty water freezes at a lower temperature than pure water.» Here pure means water with nothing added to it.
explain: Pure can also mean clean, with no dirt, germs or harmful things, as in «pure air». Pure can mean complete or total, as in «pure luck» or «pure joy». To check which meaning fits, swap in another word: «pure luck» becomes «total luck», and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Sometimes the context tells you that pure means only, with nothing else mixed in. «Some answers came first from pure reasoning» means the answers came from thinking alone. Look at the words around pure, then try your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Pure means not mixed with anything else.
fact: Pure water has no taste, smell or colour, and it boils at 100 °C.
fact: Tap water is safe to drink but not totally pure.
fact: «Pure orange juice» means nothing has been added to the juice.
fact: Mixtures can be separated by filtering, sieving or evaporating to get purer substances.
exercise: «Inside your phone is a computer chip printed onto silicon, which comes from sand made extremely pure.» What does pure mean here? | *Not mixed with anything else | Very loud | Bright red | Full of holes
exercise: «Winning the prize was pure luck.» What does pure mean here? | Made of two things mixed together | Dirty and muddy | Slow and steady | *Complete or total
exercise: Which of these is a pure substance, made of only one thing? | Tap water | Air | *Pure gold | Salt water
test: Pure water boils at what temperature? | 50 °C | 200 °C | *100 °C | 0 °C
test: A carton says «pure orange juice». What does this mean? | *Nothing has been added to it | Sugar has been added to it | It is made from apples | It has been frozen solid
exam: Which statement about tap water is true? | Tap water is a pure substance made of only one thing | Tap water boils at 50 °C | *Tap water is safe but not totally pure | Tap water is totally pure
